{"id":1395,"date":"2020-11-27T15:49:00","date_gmt":"2020-11-27T23:49:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1395"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:31","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:31","slug":"rokit-conditionals","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/rokit-conditionals\/","title":{"rendered":"Conditionals"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221604292d1\" name=\"6a221604292d1\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Briefing video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]If you would like an explanation on if statements, watch this video. Else, move on to the steps below or another lesson.[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=vxSFhV223JE&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221604293e6\" name=\"6a221604293e6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What are if statements?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<em>If statements<\/em>\u00a0let our code make decisions. We use them all the time in our lives! For example:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>If it is sunny, I will go outside.<\/li>\n<li>If I am thirsty, I will drink some water.<\/li>\n<li>If my cat is clawing me, then I will stop pulling on its tail.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">if (condition)\r\n{\r\n    \/\/then action\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>The\u00a0<em>condition\u00a0<\/em>(inside of the parentheses) is the &#8220;if&#8221; part, and inside of the curly braces is the &#8220;then&#8221; part. The first part of one of our examples would look like this:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">if (it is sunny)\r\n{\r\n    \/\/then I will go outside\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22160429454\" name=\"6a22160429454\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Else statement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Now that you know what an if statement is, you can write an actual program using variables and if statements. Create variable A with a value of 12 and an if statement to see if it&#8217;s larger than 10. If it is, variable A will be set to 10.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int A = 12; if (A &gt; 10){    \r\n    A = 10}<\/pre>\n<p>Now you can add an else statement, which will be performed if the if statement turns out to be false:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">if (condition)\r\n{\r\n    \/\/happens if condition is true\r\n}\r\nelse\r\n{\r\n    \/\/happens if condition is false\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>Create an else statement so A will be set to 1 if it is not larger than 10. Your code should look like this:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int A = 12;\r\nif (A &gt; 10)\r\n{\r\n    A = 10;\r\n}\r\nelse\r\n{\r\n    A = 1;\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221604294d7\" name=\"6a221604294d7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Else if statement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You can combine everything together into an else if statement:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int A = 3;\r\n\r\nif (A &gt; 10)\r\n{\r\n    A = 10;\r\n}\r\nelse if (A &lt; 5)\r\n{\r\n    A = 1;\r\n}\r\nelse\r\n{\r\n    A = 9;\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>The pseudocode, or the description of what the computer is reading, is:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>If A is greater than 10 it will equal 10.<\/li>\n<li>If A is not greater than 10 and less than 5, it will equal 1.<\/li>\n<li>If A is not greater than 10 and not less than 5, it will equal 9<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>For these\u00a0<em>conditions\u00a0<\/em>you have several comparison options using mathematical symbols:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Greater than: &gt;<\/li>\n<li>Less than: &lt;<\/li>\n<li>Greater than or equal to: &gt;=<\/li>\n<li>Less than or equal to: &lt;=<\/li>\n<li>Equal to: ==<\/li>\n<li>Not equal to: !=<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22160429550\" name=\"6a22160429550\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Create your own code, or try this one out:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int A = 1; \/\/ create A\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n    Serial.begin(9600); \/\/ starts the serial monitor\r\n}\r\n \r\nvoid loop() {\r\n    \/\/ prints out the value of A\r\n    Serial.print(\"A = \");\r\n    Serial.println(A);\r\n\r\n    if( A &gt; 10) \/\/ if A is greater than 10\r\n    {\r\n        A = 0; \/\/ set A to 0\r\n    }\r\n    else if( A == 1) \/\/ otherwise if A equals 1\r\n    {\r\n        A = 3; \/\/ set A to 3\r\n    }\r\n    else \/\/ otherwise\r\n    {\r\n    A = A + 1; \/\/ add one to A\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    delay(100);\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>When you run this code on the serial monitor, it should output:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>A = 1<\/li>\n<li>A = 3<\/li>\n<li>A = 4<\/li>\n<li>A = 5<\/li>\n<li>A = 6<\/li>\n<li>A = 7<\/li>\n<li>A = 8<\/li>\n<li>A = 9<\/li>\n<li>A = 10<\/li>\n<li>A = 11<\/li>\n<li>A = 0<\/li>\n<li>A = 1<\/li>\n<li>A = 3<\/li>\n<li>A = 4<\/li>\n<li>etc.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Since A is set to 1, the computer will go to the else if part and add 1. A will then become 3. 1 will keep being added to A until A is greater than 10. Once that happens, A will be set to 0 and the cycle will be repeated.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 6 Briefing video [vc_column_text]If you would like an explanation on if statements, watch this video. Else, move on to the steps below or another lesson.[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=vxSFhV223JE\" align=\"center\"] [\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/rokit-conditionals\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1735,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1814,1760,1737],"lesson-tag":[2163,2123,2182,2186,2122,2171],"class_list":["post-1395","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-fundamentals","lesson-tag-if-statements","lesson-tag-mouse","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","module-mouse","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1395","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1395\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":6617,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1395\/revisions\/6617"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1735"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1395"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1395"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1395"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}